In article <bqpocv$2bk$1@phys-news1.kolumbus.fi>, gh01@onetel.net.uk 
says...

> I'm new to all this.  I have a few questions.

Welcome to the bunch... You'll see we are most helpful. Almost no spam 
or trolls here either (and those that get through get *special* fun 
treatment which can be a hilarious read).

 
> 1. is there a FAQ somewhere that I can get answers to these?

Uh oh, several. Others can probably point you in more exact directions 
but for now:
1) you have read the guidebook coming with the installation, haven't 
you?
2) try http://www.nethack.de/, especially the hints section
3) http://home.tiscali.nl/~bwaijers has a lot too

And beware, don't read too much in advance. The game is big enough not 
to get spoiled but it's so much fun to realize... they thought of this 
TOO. Furthermore, it's not "bad" to read spoilers, most people here 
would never have ascended (won once) without it.

 
> 2. Are female characters immune to seduction attacks by nymphs?

Nope. Sex has very little relevance in nh. A few monsters like succubus 
are attracted to males and incubus to females. Females can lay eggs. 
Females can kick sinks for special effects (I wish they just did the 
dishes). You'll probably have a bit more fun playing a female 
character.

 
> 3. I've read about mine-town on the group.  Is this the place in the mines
> where there are watchmen, an altar with a priest(ess), and a couple of
> shops?  I found this once, but I did something to annoy the watchmen and
> they came after me.  I killed three of them, but the watch-captain got me.
> Was it picking the locked doors?  The whistle seemed to be blown when I
> drank from one of the fountains... guess I'll have to experiment some more
> with that.

That's it. There are several things there you "shouldn't" do like 
picking locks, kicking doors, stopping the water flow in the fountains 
(and robbing shops :-). Until you feel more comfortable with the game, 
just behave like you would in real life.
 

> 4. Bones levels.... I occasionally come across these, but of course, since
> there is only me that plays on this machine, I only ever see old versions of
> myself, with associated pets and stuff.  Is there some way of sharing bones
> files with other players through the internet?  On this subject, is it
> possible to kill ghosts by conventional means, but just difficult because
> they have a low AC (as far as I have seen), or can this not be done?

You can play on the net... or go to one of the bones file sharing 
servers (don't remember any now, you can probably find references at 
that nethack.de site).
Ghosts can be killed "normally", it just takes a while unless you are a 
killing machine (enough exp and equipment).
 

>  5. Someone mentioned someting about identifying wands by engraving?  Is
> there something particular I should engrave?  I read about the E word on the
> group, but I think that is only for scaring monsters?

You can engrave anything, like "x". The main thing is what happens when 
you do. A wand of cold will drop some icecubes, a wand of fire will 
burn the text into the floor etc. Some wands will do nothing (so you 
have to zap them at things to figure those out).

All this can be found in spoilers and hints... but go easy on those...

 
> I am sure there are many, many more questions I could ask... this game is
> BIG.

Be prepared, several months of your life will now be spent entirely 
within the dungeon. Lots of us play after years, even decades.


Happy hacking, 
